    {
      "id": "9520850",
      "title": "Working with \"overflow\" and Relative Positioning",
      "lectureOrder": 90,
      "videoOrder": 79,
      "sourceHash": "53832b964f8e2d53dd2c3363b231471d2832caad517e07c88d5f09d4a44d4789",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.17,
          "end": 9.85,
          "en": "So we saw how relative positioning works and we also saw that we can move our element out of the parent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 10.45,
          "end": 12.11,
          "en": "Now to avoid this behavior,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 12.19,
          "end": 22.56,
          "en": "we can simply go to our parent element with the class parent right here and now add overflow hidden because this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 22.56,
          "end": 27.09,
          "en": "will exactly do what the property already indicates,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 27.33,
          "end": 32.57,
          "en": "it will hide the element once it's outside of our parent, like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 32.7,
          "end": 39.57,
          "en": "as you can see it. If we would reuse the top distance now, maybe 2, I'm not sure,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 39.57,
          "end": 43.69,
          "en": "this is like trial and error or maybe 80, something like that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 43.71,
          "end": 44.49,
          "en": "let's see,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 44.82,
          "end": 46.52,
          "en": "yes we can see it already,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 46.62,
          "end": 51.94,
          "en": "as soon as the element moves out of the parent element, it's invisible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 51.96,
          "end": 57.84,
          "en": "This can be a behavior you want or not but at least it allows you to make sure that you don't place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 57.9,
          "end": 61.07,
          "en": "elements anywhere on your website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 61.08,
          "end": 62.76,
          "en": "Now there is one problem though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 62.85,
          "end": 67.5,
          "en": "I mentioned that in the last video. If I remove the overflow",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 67.5,
          "end": 69.88,
          "en": "hidden property right here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 70.14,
          "end": 72.11,
          "en": "and also remove position relative",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 72.15,
          "end": 76.43,
          "en": "and actually all the code we have for our child, like that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 76.51,
          "end": 87.3,
          "en": "let's now say that our parent is now a relatively positioned element, like that and also pushed down",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 87.3,
          "end": 90.72,
          "en": "from the top by maybe 200 pixels.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 90.75,
          "end": 97.2,
          "en": "What happens now is that if I reload the page, you could guess that, is that element is now outside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 97.28999999999999,
          "end": 103.33,
          "en": "of the parent, so the parent of our parent right here is the body element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 103.35,
          "end": 104.74000000000001,
          "en": "We can see this right here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 104.97,
          "end": 107.78,
          "en": "we have the div class parent inside the body,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 107.82,
          "end": 110.03,
          "en": "so body is the parent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 110.09,
          "end": 113.14,
          "en": "and now you could say well I can solve this easily,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 113.16,
          "end": 119.38,
          "en": "the only thing I have to do is I have to go to the body selector right here and add overflow",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 119.49000000000001,
          "end": 121.82,
          "en": "hidden like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 121.86,
          "end": 123.16,
          "en": "Let's see if this works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 123.45,
          "end": 129.69,
          "en": "as you can imagine by my voice, it probably won't work because if I unselect the inspect tool and reload the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 129.69,
          "end": 134.6,
          "en": "page, you can see I can reload it as often as I want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 134.63,
          "end": 136.32,
          "en": "nothing changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 136.93,
          "end": 138.14,
          "en": "and why is this happening?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 138.32,
          "end": 144.92000000000002,
          "en": "Well this is due to a default behavior of CSS. If you apply the overflow",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 144.92000000000002,
          "end": 147.71,
          "en": "hidden declaration to the body element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 147.71,
          "end": 151.65,
          "en": "this will simply be passed onto the HTML element right here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 151.66,
          "end": 159.68,
          "en": "so in our case to the HTML selector and the consequence of that is, well you don't have the overflow hidden declaration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 159.77,
          "end": 161,
          "en": "on your body element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 161.24,
          "end": 163.7,
          "en": "so the code you basically have is this one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 163.7,
          "end": 166.15,
          "en": "You can cut this out, add it right here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 166.22,
          "end": 167.27,
          "en": "save the file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 167.27,
          "end": 172.1,
          "en": "so you have overflow hidden on the HTML element but not on the body element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 172.13,
          "end": 175.92000000000002,
          "en": "and if we have a look at our page now, this is the consequence,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 176,
          "end": 179.43,
          "en": "you don't have any impact of this declaration at all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 180.57,
          "end": 183.61,
          "en": "This is just a default behavior of CSS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 183.63,
          "end": 185.49,
          "en": "as I said, so we cannot change that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 185.49,
          "end": 191.19,
          "en": "unfortunately. What we can do though is we can simply take the chance and also add overflow",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 191.18,
          "end": 193.97,
          "en": "hidden to our body element right here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 194.25,
          "end": 202.62,
          "en": "If we do that and reload the page, we can see that the overflow property is working again because right",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 202.65,
          "end": 210.24,
          "en": "now, the overflow hidden declaration is not passed onto the HTML element because it already has such",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 210.24,
          "end": 211.19,
          "en": "a declaration,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 211.2,
          "end": 213.02,
          "en": "why would it need it twice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 213.06,
          "end": 214.07,
          "en": "doesn't make sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 214.23,
          "end": 216.41,
          "en": "and because of that, this is working.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 216.51,
          "end": 222.15,
          "en": "It would also work if you add overflow auto by the way here, as you can see, same behavior,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 222.36,
          "end": 228.66,
          "en": "the element cannot be displayed outside the parent which is the body element in our case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 228.66,
          "end": 234.38,
          "en": "This is just some quick tip that I wanted to show you in case you have a situation like that. If your",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 234.39,
          "end": 236.35,
          "en": "parent is not the body element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 236.4,
          "end": 237.82999999999998,
          "en": "this is not a problem at all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 237.99,
          "end": 243.64,
          "en": "but if this is the case, then you can solve this issue with this little fix right here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 243.75,
          "end": 247.82,
          "en": "With that, we now understood the relative positioning,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 247.95,
          "end": 252.97,
          "en": "so there is only one value left that we should have a look at, sticky positioning.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 253.26,
          "end": 255.88,
          "en": "Let's see how this works in the next video.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
